WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.894 --> 00:00:16.978
will be kind to visitors," Onatah's grandmother said.

2
00:00:16.998 --> 00:00:20.681
"These two can join the festival after Busk."

3
00:00:21.922 --> 00:00:25.045
She gave Onatah some old animal skins.

4
00:00:25.065 --> 00:00:27.868
"Put these in the fire."

5
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.062
The children walked over to the large fire.

6
00:00:32.082 --> 00:00:35.545
"What is Busk?"

7
00:00:36.105 --> 00:00:36.845
Vinnie asked.

8
00:00:36.865 --> 00:00:43.830
"During the Green Corn Festival, we clean our homes completely," said Onatah.

9
00:00:44.931 --> 00:00:47.093
"We burn everything we do not use."

10
00:00:48.353 --> 00:00:51.015
Onatah threw the skins into the fire.

11
00:00:52.736 --> 00:00:54.318
People were staring at them.

12
00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:55.959
"Who are they?"

13
00:00:56.639 --> 00:00:57.560
asked one man.

14
00:00:59.212 --> 00:01:02.154
"Vinnie and Mandy," shrugged Onatah.

15
00:01:02.174 --> 00:01:04.576
"Grandmother welcomed them."

16
00:01:04.596 --> 00:01:10.219
"Then you are guests of the Onondaga," said the man.

17
00:01:10.239 --> 00:01:13.622
"Onondaga?" asked Mandy.

18
00:01:14.903 --> 00:01:20.626
The girl nodded proudly: "We are Onondaga, the People of the Hills.

19
00:01:21.687 --> 00:01:23.408
But Magua is Mohawk."

20
00:01:23.969 --> 00:01:25.349
She pointed to the man.

21
00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:32.358
"Five Indian nations make up the Iroquois, the People of the Longhouse," said Magua.

22
00:01:33.419 --> 00:01:34.980
He held up one hand.

23
00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:43.305
He counted five fingers: "Oneida, Cayuga, Onondaga, Seneca, and Mohawk."

24
00:01:43.325 --> 00:01:45.687
"Five nations?"

25
00:01:46.487 --> 00:01:47.188
asked Vinnie.

26
00:01:47.208 --> 00:01:51.931
"Yes, five nations became one people—the Iroquois!"

27
00:01:52.672 --> 00:01:56.094
said Magua, closing his hand into a fist.

28
00:01:56.114 --> 00:01:59.016
"Vinnie, do you like to fish?"

29
00:02:00.364 --> 00:02:02.625
"I've never tried it," said Vinnie.

30
00:02:02.645 --> 00:02:06.367
"I'll teach you how we fish," said Magua.

31
00:02:06.387 --> 00:02:08.828
"Is it safe to split up?"

32
00:02:09.448 --> 00:02:10.688
Mandy asked Vinnie.

33
00:02:10.708 --> 00:02:13.990
"It'll be fine," said Vinnie.

34
00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.691
He followed Magua.

35
00:02:15.711 --> 00:02:20.893
"Come," said Onatah, warming to her new friend.

36
00:02:20.913 --> 00:02:23.134
"I'll show you around.

37
00:02:23.574 --> 00:02:24.914
Then we'll go to my house."

38
00:02:26.195 --> 00:02:28.236
They walked past the longhouses.

39
00:02:29.704 --> 00:02:32.966
Mandy saw an animal sign above every door.

40
00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:36.027
"What do these signs mean?"

41
00:02:36.627 --> 00:02:37.208
she asked.

42
00:02:37.228 --> 00:02:40.849
"Iroquois people belong to different clans.

43
00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:49.313
Clans are like big families that grow from one woman born long ago," explained Onatah.

44
00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:52.475
"Every clan has its own longhouse.

45
00:02:53.235 --> 00:02:54.756
I belong to the Bear Clan."

46
00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.003
The girls arrived at Onatah's longhouse and went inside.

47
00:03:01.023 --> 00:03:05.827
"Let's make a corn husk doll," suggested Onatah.

48
00:03:06.748 --> 00:03:10.171
She gave Mandy some corn hanging from the ceiling.

49
00:03:11.332 --> 00:03:14.955
Mandy also saw floor mats made from corn husks.

50
00:03:14.975 --> 00:03:19.378
"Is corn your main crop?"

51
00:03:20.079 --> 00:03:20.900
Mandy asked.

52
00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:27.625
"It is one of three vegetables we call the Three Sisters," Onatah replied.

53
00:03:27.645 --> 00:03:33.147
"Beans, squash, and corn must grow together as sisters do."

54
00:03:35.568 --> 00:03:37.849
Mandy and Onatah husked the corn.

55
00:03:37.869 --> 00:03:43.391
"Let's get some beaver skin for a doll dress," said Onatah.

56
00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:46.272
The girls ran out the door.

57
00:03:48.593 --> 00:03:51.034
Vinnie and Magua got into a canoe.

58
00:03:52.855 --> 00:03:55.796
They paddled out on a nearby stream.

59
00:03:57.072 --> 00:03:59.673
"This is for you," said Magua.

60
00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:05.296
He gave Vinnie a long spear that was in the canoe.

61
00:04:05.316 --> 00:04:09.577
"You catch fish with this?"

62
00:04:10.418 --> 00:04:12.939
asked Vinnie, looking at his spear.

63
00:04:12.959 --> 00:04:16.400
"Watch," smiled Magua.

64
00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.702
He carefully aimed his spear and quickly pierced a fish.

65
00:04:20.722 --> 00:04:25.404
"Wow!" yelled Vinnie.

66
00:04:26.044 --> 00:04:27.846
"Is this how everyone does it?"

67
00:04:29.147 --> 00:04:32.950
"Only when we fish alone or with a friend," said Magua.

68
00:04:34.211 --> 00:04:36.573
"Mostly, we use the fish traps we've built."

69
00:04:37.533 --> 00:04:38.414
"Fish traps?"

70
00:04:39.055 --> 00:04:39.895
asked Vinnie.

71
00:04:39.915 --> 00:04:48.462
"The stream guides the fish into the trap," said Magua, pointing to a large circular dam made out

72
00:04:48.502 --> 00:04:49.103
of sticks.

73
00:04:49.123 --> 00:04:51.885
"Then we use a net to catch them."

74
00:04:53.006 --> 00:04:55.188
"Why are you in the Onondaga village?"

75
00:04:55.832 --> 00:04:56.553
asked Vinnie.

76
00:04:56.573 --> 00:04:58.854
"I am only visiting.

77
00:04:59.395 --> 00:05:03.077
My people live toward the rising sun," said Magua.

78
00:05:03.097 --> 00:05:05.919
"We are the Keepers of the Eastern Door.

79
00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.902
Mohawks protect the Iroquois from the whites in the East."

80
00:05:11.022 --> 00:05:14.665
Raising his spear, Magua moved with great speed.

81
00:05:15.766 --> 00:05:18.527
Then he speared another big fish.
